IO-35: default REPORT_START_TIME to 00:00:00 instead of NO_DATE

setDefaults() initialised both ReportStartDate and ReportStartTime to NO_DATE
(-693594 days). With REPORT_START_DATE given and REPORT_START_TIME omitted,
project_readInput() formed ReportStart = date - 693594 days, which
MAX(ReportStart, StartDateTime) replaced by the simulation start, so the
requested report start date was ignored. Default the time to 00:00:00, as the
input reference documents. When REPORT_START_DATE is omitted the sum is still
before the simulation start, so reporting still begins with the simulation.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-35_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/project.c b/src/legacy/engine/project.c
index d24c17f..cc887ba 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/project.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/project.c
@@ -920,7 +920,7 @@ void setDefaults()
    EndDate         = StartDate;
    EndTime         = 0.0;
    ReportStartDate = NO_DATE;
-   ReportStartTime = NO_DATE;
+   ReportStartTime = 0.0;              // 00:00:00 on REPORT_START_DATE
    SweepStart      = 1;
    SweepEnd        = 365;
 
